{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaaty/mobile_work_door

    A door of «Your work» (local\yourwork): a service the person runs, with its logo on its light plate, how many things
    of it are waiting (red if one is urgent), its name and a line of how it is. The whole door opens the service.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title, status, icon - The service; short (from the home's context) for its line in whole parts, statusshort.
    * hasalerts, alertcount, alertlabel, urgent - What of it is waiting.
    * url, browser - Its main page, a page of the web: in the app's window, signed in, never through a plugin's handler of
      links (those are for the notices to readers and families, and may take a staff page to a reader's one); in the
      phone's browser for the pages a plugin wants there.

    A door without a title is none: the example, empty, draws nothing, because what the app compiles is not HTML that the
    checks of the templates take.

    Example context (json):
    {}
}}
{{#title}}
<a class="aty-puerta{{#urgent}} aty-urgent{{/urgent}}" core-link href="{{url}}" capture="false"{{^browser}} inApp="true"{{/browser}}>
    <span class="aty-puerta-cab">
        <span class="aty-servicio-logo">{{#icon}}<img src="{{icon}}" alt="">{{/icon}}</span>
        {{#hasalerts}}<span class="aty-puerta-avisos" aria-label="{{alertlabel}}">{{alertcount}}</span>{{/hasalerts}}
    </span>
    <span class="aty-puerta-nombre">{{title}}</span>
    {{#short}}{{#statusshort}}<span class="aty-puerta-estado">{{statusshort}}</span>{{/statusshort}}{{/short}}
    {{^short}}{{#status}}<span class="aty-puerta-estado">{{status}}</span>{{/status}}{{/short}}
</a>
{{/title}}
